+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"Done. All validation passes: `npm run build` compiles clean, `npm run lint` has no errors, and all **45/45 tests pass** (verified across two runs).\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/models.ts` — `Document`, `Version`, and `Operation` (insert/delete) interfaces.\n- `src/db.ts` — `createDatabase(dbPath)` factory; loads `schema.sql` (works from both `src/` and `dist/`), enables WAL + foreign keys, clears `active_connections` on startup so restarts start fresh.\n- `src/ot.ts` — `applyOperation`, `transformOperation` (position shifting for inserts, overlap-aware shrinking for delete-vs-delete, tie-break favors the already-applied op), and `validateOperation` with strict bounds checking.\n- `src/routes.ts` — full CRUD plus version history; creating a doc seeds version 0, and each WS edit inserts a new row, so any past version is retrievable.\n- `src/ws.ts` — one room per document with in-memory state (`version`, `content`, pending op log). Incoming ops are transformed against every op committed after the client's base version, then applied in a SQLite transaction, acked to the sender, and broadcast to the rest of the room. Connections are tracked in `active_connections` and removed on close.\n- `src/server.ts` — `createApp(dbPath?)` combining Express + WS on one HTTP server/port, with `start(port?)` resolving the actual port and `stop()` terminating sockets, closing the server, and closing the DB.\n\n**Key design choice**: message handling is serialized per connection through a promise queue and current state is re-read per operation, which keeps the 50 rapid-fire edits and 10-client stress tests corruption-free without any locking complexity."}}
